## Team Contribution

This lab was completed individually by me, Jaya Vyas. I researched how KVM handles VM-exits, implemented the per-exit counters and periodic printk in the Intel VMX path, resolved kernel build issues, built and installed the modified kernel/module on the outer VM, enabled nested virtualization, and validated the output by booting and exercising the inner VM.

---

## Overview

This assignment implements VM-exit statistics tracking in the Linux KVM subsystem for Intel VMX. The patch adds:

- Per-exit-type atomic counters
- Periodic statistics printing to kernel logs
- Exit reason naming for better debugging

### Quick Start Summary

- Clone the Linux repository into the outer VM
- Install build dependencies and configure the kernel using the current config
- Add swap space to ensure smooth kernel build
- Fix build errors related to trusted keys and recompile
- Modify `arch/x86/kvm/vmx/vmx.c` to add exit statistics counters and printing logic
- Build and install the modified KVM modules
- Reboot and verify the patch with dmesg and nested VM testing

---

## Detailed Steps

### Step 1: Kernel Build Test on the Outer VM

#### a) Clone your GitHub fork onto the outer VM and prepare dependencies

```bash
git clone https://github.com/jayavyas07/linux.git
cd linux
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y build-essential bc flex bison libssl-dev libelf-dev libncurses-dev dwarves ccache
```

![Clone and Dependencies](images/image1.png)

#### b) Seed the config from the running kernel and accept defaults

```bash
cp -v /boot/config-$(uname -r) .config
yes "" | make olddefconfig
```

![Kernel Config](images/image2.png)

#### c) (If needed) Add swap to avoid OOM during build

```bash
sudo fallocate -l 4G /swapfile && sudo chmod 600 /swapfile && sudo mkswap /swapfile && sudo swapon /swapfile
echo '/swapfile none swap sw 0 0' | sudo tee -a /etc/fstab
free -h
```

*Figure 1: System memory after enabling swap (pre-build)*

![Swap Setup](images/image3.png)

#### d) Build the kernel and modules

```bash
make -j"$(nproc)" 2>&1 | tee build.log
```

*Figure 2: Kernel build in progress / bzImage generation*

![Kernel Build](images/image4.png)

#### e) Install and boot the test kernel to confirm it runs

```bash
sudo make modules_install
sudo make install
sudo update-initramfs -c -k $(make kernelrelease)
sudo update-grub
sudo reboot
```

*Figure 3: Post-reboot verification and environment checks*

![Post-reboot Verification](images/image5.png)

![Environment Checks](images/image6.png)

