## Frequency of Exits

The total exit count increases steadily over time but not at a perfectly constant rate. Spikes occur during:

- CPU feature discovery (e.g., CPUID)
- MSR accesses
- Memory management events (e.g., EPT violations), especially during boot

Once the guest is idle, exit rate stabilizes. In my measurements, a full VM boot generated approximately **400K–500K total exits**.

---

## Exit-Type Frequency (Most vs Least)

| Exit Type | Meaning | Observed Frequency | Context / Notes |
|-----------|---------|-------------------|-----------------|
| CPUID (9) | CPU feature query | Very frequent | During kernel/userspace init and library probing |
| HLT (12) | Guest idle loop | Frequent | When waiting for interrupts / scheduler idle |
| RDMSR/WRMSR (30/31) | Model-specific register access | Moderate | System setup and drivers |
| EPT_VIOLATION (48) | MMU translation fault | Common | Boot/memory mapping activity |
| EPT_MISCONFIG (49) | Invalid EPT mapping | Occasional | Early boot / misconfig paths |
| UNKNOWN | Unlabeled exit reasons | Rare | Any exit not explicitly named in the switch |

